Z||000010||Bob Englert||07-14-2001||09:42 PM||||Chris:<P>I was planning to drive over until about 7:30 Friday evening when my forward exhaust manifold developed a very noticeable exhaust leak.  I had just picked up an extra ignition module for the trip when it appeared as I was leaving Advance Auto.  Since it would be almost 6 hours each way I couldn't take the chance to have it really open up far from home.  <P>At this point I doubt I will be able to bring it to Williamsburg since I won't have near enough time to get it repaired before the show.<P>A real bummer since it was a great day for a drive.<P>Now the car sits in the garage until I can get time to fix it.<P>It was not a good Friday the 13th for me!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroHarry||07-14-2001||10:19 PM||||Damn sorry to here about that Bob, you better try and make Williamsburg though....<BR>Hey are we still game for RFTH6 ?<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 266K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||07-14-2001||10:43 PM||||Hey, Bob, you gonna try to repair or replace that manifold?  It's for forward one, isn't it?  (just about has to be, you know?)<P>If we can scrounge up a good manifold, maybe we can get you running in time for Williamsburg.  Missing Kitty Hawk was bad enough - we gotta get you rolling for Williamsburg!<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000013||qwikgta||07-14-2001||11:01 PM||||Chris and the NC gang.<BR>  I Just got back from the Kitty Hawk tour, And WE DID SHOW. We had a time change that I thought was passed to all members.  We made it and we hung out for over TWO hours waiting for anyone to show.  Then we went to the Brewery and then to dinner.  No show.  Only one NC guy made it and he did after missing one of the two ferrys he had to take to get there.  <BR>  I feel the pain Chris, I waited for this too, I spend many hours getting my ride ready for it and even redid my work schedule too.  Not to say it was a total bust, we did have some great chow and BEER.  We talked about doing it agian in Sept/Oct when the weather is cooler (not cold).   <P>  Anyway see you all at Williamsburg in a few weeks<P>Rob   <P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Bob Englert||07-14-2001||11:04 PM||||I need to see exactly where the problem is before I can decide.  If it is cracked at a seam than I will probably replace it.  I don't yet know where the leak is but I could feel the exhaust when I stuck my hand down between the firewall and the front manifold.<P>I will be leaving for FL on Sunday to visit Megan at Embry-Riddle.  She is between classes down there.  Will be back Wednesday evening for my MCSE certification class.  Hopefully I will be able to get a look at exactly what the problem is next weekend.<P>I will be going to RFTH6 even if I have to drive Megan's 4cyl automatic coupe!<P>BTW: RFTH6 will be September 21st - 23rd at Cherokee, NC<P><BR>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
